# Z3FDB Profiling

This contains the tools and scripts that I have developed to run Z3FDB profiling. They are not polished and required code changes in some places if you want to swap configuration.

This folder contains:

```
├── data                <- Contains profiling configurations
├── hpc-jobs            <- SLURM Jobs to prep & run profiling on ATOS
├── requirements.txt    <- requirements for this tool   
├── z3fdb_profiler      <- code
└── z3fdb-profiler      <- entry point
```

## High Level Overview

For a performance comparison / profiling run you will need a FDB with the appropriate data.

*Setup FDB (Alternative A)*

If you want to run simulate machine learning training use you will need to first download ERA5 data from MARS. Use `hpc-jobs/download/download-era.data.py` to download, this will require `earthkit-data`. You will need to modify the script if you want to change the data that is downloaded. *BE AWARE: The downloaded data needs to fit the requests use later*

*Operational FDB (Alternative B)*
If you want to work with current forecast data you can simply use the production fdb config on ATOS. *BE AWARE that you need to rely on relative dates or your will ru into issues when data gets purged*

*Native Zarr Stores*
To export a zarr store from FDB use `z3fdb-profiler`. See `z3fdb-profiler export --help` for all options. For a fair comparison you should probably use lz4 with default settings. Be sure to work on scratch to ensure you run with LUSTRE underneath.

See `hpc-jobs/jobs/export_*` jobs

*Benchmarking*
Each of the benchmarking jobs runs 100 HPC jobs and reports the time taken. Use this to compare wall time needed to read from Z3FDB vs. Native Zarr.

*Profiling*
Creates a Flamegraph from perf profiles, run `hpc-jobs/jobs/profile-z3fdb.sh`, requires https://github.com/brendangregg/flamegraph to be cloned (update location in job)

